          "source_text_sha256": "98d39dc740f60a6bf1a96a74c586ffc623be038198f518a3682f560898bc9eea",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On November 27, 2013, at 6:00 PM, two individuals observed an intermittent light phenomenon in the sky. The observation lasted 1.5 hours and was divided into three phases:\n\n- A stationary bright light to the northeast (two large yellow headlights with a red light in the middle) that then disappeared behind a building, reminiscent of a plane or helicopter seen face-on with its lights on.\n\n- The son of the witness observed a bright point of light passing over the house that \"wobbled.\" At 6:02 PM and 6:05 PM, two aircraft flew over the area at high altitude (refer to Flightradar records and the military radar trace on the Geoportail map in local time). There was also activity from a helicopter at that time, between 6:12 PM and 6:30 PM, flying over the high-voltage line between Quinssaines and Nouhant, 7 km southwest of the observation location. The witness's description is not precise enough to determine what aircraft was actually observed.\n\n- For the end of the observation, a very bright point to the southwest, almost fixed for over an hour: this is undoubtedly the planet Venus, which is particularly bright at this time (Magnitude -4.7). The variety of the witness's photos can be explained by inconsistent focus settings and camera movement.\n\nThe GEIPAN classifies this case as \"A\": observation of Venus for the end of the observation, and probable observation of planes and/or helicopters for the beginning of the observation.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "441648c2448c8bcc572315215b72bb805c74f94828330663e1c8273b303f79d4"
        }
      ],
